Package: [[package.name]]
# Not [[version]]: that is the raw Maven version, and apt compares on this line. This is the reader's version with
# -SNAPSHOT rewritten to ~snapshot.<run>, which sorts below the release rather than above it.
Version: [[reader.package.version]]
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Michael Schnell <michael@fuin.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/porelo-ai/porelo-adapters
# The native binary links against both; jdeb does not read it to find out. check-linkage holds these floors to it.
Depends: porelo, libc6 (>= [[package.glibc.floor]]), zlib1g (>= 1:[[package.zlib.floor]])
Description: Porelo's build reader for Forgejo Actions
 Reads a task's builds on Forgejo Actions for Porelo: which runs a pushed commit
 started, how they ended, and the logs of the jobs that failed. Installs into
 /usr/libexec/porelo/builds as 'forgejo', where porelo finds the reader a project
 names with 'builds: { forge: forgejo }'. Nothing needs to be registered.
